From: Brad House <bhouse@nexthop.ai>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zebra: keep a retired neighbour inactive when its MAC is re-sent

zebra_evpn_process_neigh_on_local_mac_change() re-sends every local
neighbour of a MAC when the MAC's sequence number or ES changes, and clears
ZEBRA_NEIGH_LOCAL_INACTIVE on each. It runs for a sync MAC update from an ES
peer that carries a new sequence number, and for a neighbour that is
relinked to the MAC or moves to it from remote, which bumps the MAC's
sequence number. If the MAC has already left the local dataplane, neither
is evidence that the host is back, yet every neighbour the inactive walker
retired is advertised as a non-proxy MAC-IP route again. With reachable-only
advertisement disabled nothing marks them inactive afterwards, so the peers'
hold timers stay cancelled and the MAC is never withdrawn.

Apply the rule the neighbour update paths use: with reachable-only
advertisement disabled, a neighbour of a locally inactive MAC keeps its
inactive state. It is re-sent with the new sequence number only while it is
ready for BGP, which makes it a proxy route when a peer still reports it
active, and is left withdrawn otherwise. Reachable-only mode and the
neighbours of an active MAC are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Brad House <bhouse@nexthop.ai>
---
diff --git a/zebra/zebra_evpn_neigh.c b/zebra/zebra_evpn_neigh.c
index c807ce5aa5..c5076b9840 100644
--- a/zebra/zebra_evpn_neigh.c
+++ b/zebra/zebra_evpn_neigh.c
@@ -980,6 +980,10 @@ void zebra_evpn_process_neigh_on_local_mac_change(struct zebra_evpn *zevpn,
 	struct zebra_neigh *n = NULL;
 	struct listnode *node = NULL;
 	struct zebra_vrf *zvrf = NULL;
+	bool keep_retired;
+	bool frozen;
+	bool old_bgp_ready;
+	bool new_bgp_ready;
 
 	zvrf = zevpn->vxlan_if->vrf->info;
 
@@ -988,6 +992,16 @@ void zebra_evpn_process_neigh_on_local_mac_change(struct zebra_evpn *zevpn,
 			   &zmac->macaddr, seq_change ? "CHANGE" : "ADD",
 			   zevpn->vni);
 
+	/* A sequence or ES change on a MAC that has left the local dataplane
+	 * is no evidence the host is back, so a retired neighbour stays
+	 * retired and is re-sent only if a peer still reports it active.
+	 */
+	keep_retired = zebra_evpn_neigh_local_inactive_next(
+		true /* cur_inactive */, false /* new_to_mac */,
+		false /* local_inactive */,
+		zebra_evpn_mh_do_adv_reachable_neigh_only(),
+		!!CHECK_FLAG(zmac->flags, ZEBRA_MAC_LOCAL_INACTIVE));
+
 	/* Walk all neighbors and mark any inactive local neighbors as
 	 * active and/or update sequence number upon a move, and inform BGP.
 	 * The action for remote neighbors is TBD.
@@ -998,14 +1012,32 @@ void zebra_evpn_process_neigh_on_local_mac_change(struct zebra_evpn *zevpn,
 		if (CHECK_FLAG(n->flags, ZEBRA_NEIGH_LOCAL)) {
 			if (IS_ZEBRA_NEIGH_INACTIVE(n) || seq_change
 			    || es_change) {
+				frozen = zebra_evpn_do_dup_addr_detect(zvrf) &&
+					 zvrf->dad_freeze &&
+					 CHECK_FLAG(n->flags,
+						    ZEBRA_NEIGH_DUPLICATE);
+
+				if (keep_retired &&
+				    CHECK_FLAG(n->flags,
+					       ZEBRA_NEIGH_LOCAL_INACTIVE)) {
+					old_bgp_ready =
+						zebra_evpn_neigh_is_ready_for_bgp(n);
+					ZEBRA_NEIGH_SET_ACTIVE(n);
+					n->loc_seq = zmac->loc_seq;
+					new_bgp_ready =
+						zebra_evpn_neigh_is_ready_for_bgp(n);
+					if (!frozen)
+						zebra_evpn_neigh_send_add_del_to_client(
+							n, old_bgp_ready,
+							new_bgp_ready);
+					continue;
+				}
+
 				ZEBRA_NEIGH_SET_ACTIVE(n);
 				UNSET_FLAG(n->flags,
 					   ZEBRA_NEIGH_LOCAL_INACTIVE);
 				n->loc_seq = zmac->loc_seq;
-				if (!(zebra_evpn_do_dup_addr_detect(zvrf)
-				      && zvrf->dad_freeze
-				      && !!CHECK_FLAG(n->flags,
-						      ZEBRA_NEIGH_DUPLICATE)))
+				if (!frozen)
 					zebra_evpn_neigh_send_add_to_client(
 						zevpn->vni, &n->ip, &n->emac,
 						n->mac, n->flags, n->loc_seq);
